⚽ Football Intelligence Hub
Day 19/60 — 60 Day Claude AI Challenge
An AI-powered football analysis app that runs Claude live, inside the app itself, to generate World Cup predictions, score your football IQ, and match your personality to Messi or Ronaldo.
What it does
A single-file HTML app, no backend, no build step — but powered entirely by real-time calls to the Claude API. Every prediction, every quiz question, and every personality result is generated live by Claude, not hardcoded.
The experience runs like a matchday broadcast, in four stages:
Stage
What happens
🏟️ Pre-Match
You select your football knowledge level — this calibrates the depth and language for everything that follows
⚽ 1st Half
Claude generates a FIFA World Cup 2026 prediction report: winner, runner-up, dark horse, and players to watch — each with a confidence score, supporting evidence, and risks
🟡 Half-Time
A 5-question Football IQ quiz, mixing beginner-to-advanced difficulty based on your level. Claude scores your answers and assigns a Football Awareness Score (0–100) with a fan classification
🔵 2nd Half
A 12-question personality assessment (multiple-choice + rating scale) covering ambition, leadership, creativity, decision-making, and more — without ever directly asking "Messi or Ronaldo?"
🏁 Full-Time
Everything compiles into one Football Intelligence Profile: your World Cup picks, IQ score, Messi/Ronaldo compatibility %, personality archetype, and recommended player/club/team/rivalry to explore
Why it's interesting
This isn't a static quiz with pre-written outcomes. The app calls api.anthropic.com/v1/messages directly from the browser at each stage, sends Claude structured prompts, and parses JSON responses back into the UI live. Ask it again, get a different (but reasoned) answer — same way Claude reasons in a normal conversation, just wrapped in a custom interface.
Design
Built around a "live matchday" visual language:
Palette: pitch-night green background, gold accents for prediction/prestige moments, live-green for active states
Type: Bebas Neue (scoreboard energy) for headers, Inter for body text, JetBrains Mono for scores and confidence data
Signature element: a scrolling "live commentary" feed replaces the typical loading spinner — text streams in like a football live-text feed while Claude is generating each stage's analysis
Tech
Single HTML file — vanilla JS, no framework, no build step
Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-6) called directly from the client for all analysis, scoring, and personality matching
Fully responsive, keyboard-accessible, respects prefers-reduced-motion
